WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.910
Ayumi-<i>san</i> and Ryuzoji
didn't seem like they were lying.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.980
So was that a dream?

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.120
Did I dream about that girl? And the gun?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.810
No, it was real.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.540
"Episode 2: Parallel World 
Constitutive Theorem"

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.330
Okay.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.640
Yup. It's back where it was.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.190
One more time!

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.600
So what I carry stays with me?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.630
Takuya, what is history?

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.350
Did you call me here to ask me that?

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.810
Tell me.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.360
History is the sum of everything we've done--

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.440
That's what the old ways
of thinking say about history.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.200
They say it's the memories of
how things have changed throughout time.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.080
But history is actually memories
of the process of change itself.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.330
What are you talking about?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:12.130
The concept of "history" applies even
to changes that take place to time itself.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:16.630
Not that your flea-sized brain
could comprehend that.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.260
Are you picking a fight with me?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.670
For instance,

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.510
let's say I wondered what would happen
if I hadn't eaten this piece of cake,

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.760
and went several minutes back
in time to find out.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.850
A thought experiment.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.610
What would happen then?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.020
If you asked a robot shaped like a cat,

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.440
they'd say that you'd just create a new history,
where you didn't eat the cake.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.390
And that's wrong.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.280
Let me ask you a question, then.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.110
What happened to the initial fact
that caused me to go back in time?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.700
Well... You went back in time
because you ate the cake.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.620
If you never ate the cake
in the first place, then...

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.500
Huh?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.510
Yes.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.500
The initial cause of
my choice does not disappear.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:02.560
I eat the cake, then go back into the past.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.590
A world where I don't eat the cake is born.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.360
All three of these things
are carved into history.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:14.400
"The Reflector Device is a device that
allows one to move to another parallel world."

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.290
"It is a very different beast
than a so-called 'time machine'."

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.150
Oww...

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.950
There it is again.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.360
Does something bad happen
if you use this thing too much?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.260
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.580
Were you watching that?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.490
What do you mean by "that"?

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.460
If you didn't see, it's fine.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.670
It's fine...

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.700
See you around.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.300
Summer break starts tomorrow.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.470
I want you to work as hard at
having fun as you do at your studies.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.470
Everybody, make sure to have a great time.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.520
Hey, why are we making
a diorama of Sakaimachi, anyway?

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.600
It doesn't seem very historical...

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:04.190
Dr. Arima believed that
the city itself hid a historical mystery.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.870
Yuki-<i>kun</i>, what do you 
think of Mt. Sankaku here?

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:12.160
Hmm... Well, it's a weird mountain.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.750
Yeah. It's hard to believe that erosion
from sea winds could make a shape like that,

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.040
and the place's geology is...

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:20.700
Hey.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.630
Arima-<i>kun</i>? What is it?

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.380
Do you want to join the club after all?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.280
I had a question.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.140
I came here yesterday, right?

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.640
Yes.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:36.440
You came right as we were talking
about Dr. Arima. So I remember it well.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.150
Right. You said you wanted
to borrow his research notes.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.690
I see...

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.190
Something wrong?

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.240
No, just wanted to check.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:46.800
I'm gonna borrow your phone.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.160
Hey! Don't just use our stuff!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.400
Sorry. It's urgent.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.330
Hello?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.580
Hello? What's wrong?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.290
You were talking to Ryuzoji-<i>san</i>
this morning at school, right?

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.630
What happened with my dad's research notes?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.420
I promised to send them to him.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.830
So that hasn't changed, huh?

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:12.140
No, it's nothing.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.600
Oh, right. Good timing.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.730
I wanted your help with that.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.640
My help?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.360
Kodai-<i>san</i>'s notes have a lot of
personal things mixed in with them.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.310
We need to sort through them
before the delivery people will take them.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.070
You want me to go through his notes?

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.160
Don't tell me you mean that whole room...

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.520
That's right...

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:32.780
Chief...

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.660
Sorry, things are kind 
of a mess here right now.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.470
Okay, I'll do it...

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.580
You're such a good son, boss.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.380
You're going to help me.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.510
Why me?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.670
I want to do it.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.930
I know a lot about Dr. Arima's research,
and nobody's better suited than me

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.850
to go through his things and
say what's part of his work and what isn't.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.560
It's okay, right?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.230
Yeah, I don't mind, but...

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.410
I guess you and I will 
be alone together, then.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.990
I-I'll join you!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.450
Did you see that special
on the paranormal last night?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.580
They covered our city!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.910
Of course. It was a whole 
thing about the curse.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.410
"Bizarre Incident in Sakaimachi - Brutal Murder?"
"Witness Speaks out about the Curse"
"Curse Controversy Continues Where did the limbs and head go?"
 "Unsolved Incidents... Curse... Body Part Trafficking"
 "More Strange Incidents in Sakaimachi"

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.040
The police kept getting strange reports

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.290
"Witnesses See Headless 
Corpse - Mystery Deepens"

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.290
about people being attacked
by a headless monster.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:28.460
"Body Found - Potential Murder?"

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.090
And then they found a torso
with no head or limbs.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.130
The limbs and head have yet to be found.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.720
The most likely theory is that it's
some kind of dangerous mountain cat, but...

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.510
There's a theory that 
it's zombies too, right?

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.060
That's going too far.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.020
Last night they were saying 
it might be aliens.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.230
That's ridiculous...

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.640
The lightning strikes, and then the curse...

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.030
There's a lot of weird stuff going on, huh?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.450
You never change, Mio.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.280
You're obsessed with
ancient history and the paranormal.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.160
I'm interested in both of them
from a purely scientific perspective.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.120
And it's the job of the historical
research club to solve those mysteries!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:01.970
Right!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.640
Something wrong?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.780
Oh, nothing.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.400
If you find any porn, give it to me.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.110
Not that I can imagine having
the same tastes as my dad.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.240
Wow, this one too...

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.370
Arima-<i>kun</i>?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:42.910
I'd like to make copies
before we send this to Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.420
Sure, whatever.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.420
Boss, what about this stuff?

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.010
Oh, put anything fragile over there.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.500
Sure.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.810
I knew it. He'd kept researching
the 400 Year Cycle Theory.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.810
Four hundred year cycle? What's that?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.860
The 400 Year Cycle Theory.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.770
It's a famous theory that Dr. Arima proposed.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:14.850
It's less a theory and more the
fantasy of a delusional lunatic, though.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.070
The theory remains
completely original, even today.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.490
It was so "original" that
his academic society disowned him.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.640
There's no point in talking 
to you about this.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:32.210
If only Dr. Arima was here,
he could talk some sense into his idiot son.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.210
I feel the same way.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.150
I still feel like I owe 
him a punch in the jaw.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.280
The way he just up and died on me...

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.310
I'm sorry. That was insensitive of me.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.940
Don't worry about it.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.060
I know that when you
get excited about something,

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.480
you lose track of what's going on around you.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.230
Um...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.660
So what's this 400 Year Cycle thing?

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:05.000
Oh, my dad's theory was that Japanese history
undergoes a revolution every 400 years.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.540
Around the year 1600,
they established the Edo Shogunate.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.130
Around the year 1200,
they established the Kamakura Shogunate.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.270
Around the year 800,
they moved the capital to Kyoto.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:22.390
And around the year 400, the Yamato court
unified Japan under its control.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:27.480
What's important is that in each case,
the revolution was brought by outsiders to Japan.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.850
That part isn't written
in the official histories.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:33.520
My dad's theory was that
even the ancient nations of Japan,

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.900
and our own unique culture, were brought
here by people from outside the country.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.860
Of course, he got a lot
of angry complaints from the right.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.580
The details are written here in <i>Legacy</i>.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.120
That's an impressive-looking book.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.380
You're a part of the historical research club
now, so I hope you'll read it.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.050
Of course, if you want me to, Shimazu-<i>san</i>.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.880
That thing's out of print.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.020
He's not going to be able to find a copy.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:06.020
I have multiple copies.
For collecting, for reading, and for lending.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.130
I see.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.100
We're finally done, huh?

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.440
We never did find any porn.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.030
It's still light out. 
Let's go to Mt. Sankaku.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.490
You've got way too much energy, Shimazu-<i>san</i>.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.780
What could we even do there this late?

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.740
I told you before what I was doing.
We can do more of that.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.800
Before?

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.000
You mean when you peed your bed?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.010
I did not!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.500
Not even when you were little?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.760
Well, of course I did back then...

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.210
Why are you making me say that?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.680
You mean investigate Mt. Sankaku, right?

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:44.050
Let's go!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.980
Let's go right now!

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.520
Mt. Sankaku! How exciting!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.270
Yeah...

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.940
You think so, too?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.280
Of course I do.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.450
If he finds us there'll 
be trouble. Let's hurry.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.300
Isn't that...?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.550
Hey.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.550
It's dangerous.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.770
You should stay away.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.960
Then what are you doing here, Kanna-<i>chan</i>?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.190
Goodbye.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.020
Wait, Hatano-<i>san</i>.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.000
What were you doing here?

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.220
Enjoying the wind.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:48.080
We could see you. You were doing something.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:51.500
I didn't feel well,
so I was sitting down. That's all.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.920
Hatano-<i>san</i>, are you hiding something?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:59.130
What kind of answer
would you like me to give you?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.250
You don't have to say it like that...

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:09.390
Did you put these flowers here?

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.270
They're always here when I come.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.150
You can answer that question
with a yes or a no, right?

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.400
Wait, Mio...

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.140
Goodbye.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:23.740
Wait!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.780
Knock it off.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.740
Stop!

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.440
Are you attracted to her?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.630
But Hatano-<i>san</i>'s not a good choice.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.080
What are you talking about?

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.920
There's a lot of bad rumors 
about her, you know.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:42.930
Rumors?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.680
Futago Rock has a
really weird shape, doesn't it?

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:52.060
They did radiometric dating on it once

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:55.140
and found out it's around 8,000 years old.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.190
Eight thousand years?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:00.050
That writing is older than
the four ancient civilizations, huh?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.650
Radiometric dating isn't perfect.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:07.130
Something as simple as a
meteor falling can change the results.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:13.410
All we know is that we still know
basically nothing about Mt. Sankaku.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.960
Calm down, guys...

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.330
Another guy got injured two days ago!

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.880
You want us to work on
a dangerous job site like this?

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.410
I'm just doing what the 
company tells me to...

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:29.510
You're the one who told 
us to move those rocks!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.010
No! That was Chief Arima's orders!

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.260
We're wasting time here.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.850
Let's go to Geotech and 
talk to them directly.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.230
I try to play nice,
and they act like assholes...

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.210
Hey.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.990
Looks you were feeding them
a line of crap, huh?

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.320
Oh, it's you!

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.570
What are you talking about?

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.340
You lied about Ayumi-<i>san</i>
ordering them to move those rocks.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:58.620
If I didn't say that, I 
would've been in danger.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.290
You little...

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.460
Boss?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.460
Oh, this is Flunky A, he works for Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.960
The name's Toyotomi.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.380
He films porn.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.970
I run a construction site!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.930
You told them to do it
without getting her okay, didn't you?

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.430
You got any proof?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:18.140
Nope. But it sounds extremely likely to me.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:26.110
Even if I did, it's still her responsibility
because she's my boss, right?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.740
Piece of shit...

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.990
What did you say?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.490
Nothing.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:34.670
You'd better not have
been up there on Mt. Sankaku.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:37.620
That place is off-limits.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.500
Mt. Sankaku is a public space.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.460
They finished their examination
of the lighting strikes.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:47.130
Miss, I'm sorry,
but it's under Geotech's authority now.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.720
It's dangerous.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.490
We're tearing down Futago Rock
when we expand the construction site.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:53.640
You can't do that!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.220
Mt. Sankaku is famous!

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.680
It could be declared an Important
Cultural Property by the government!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.890
Well, if you don't like it, sue.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.310
Mayor Shimazu's already given his permission,

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:07.140
and the legal application
paperwork is just about complete.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.940
Why are you tearing it down?

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:11.900
Company secret.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.360
I can't tell you.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.700
You're not even saying why,

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.850
and all you need is the Mayor's permission?

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.210
That can't be allowed to happen!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.620
Who are you, anyway?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.710
I'm Mio Shimazu. The mayor's daughter.

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:28.800
The mayor's daughter?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:33.180
I, um... I'm just doing
what the company tells me to.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.550
It's only a matter of time
before the city council approves...

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.060
Democracy is all about process!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.560
You need to get approval
before you do something, not after!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.600
I don't know what to tell you...

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.730
I'll talk to my dad personally about this.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.280
I've got to be somewhere!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.480
Bye!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.910
In the end, the good guys always win!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.080
What's his deal?

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.840
I'll ask my dad about Mt. Sankaku,

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.880
but just in case,
let's hurry up with our investigation.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:10.750
Right.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.590
Yuki, walk her home.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:13.840
Sure thing!

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.590
The hotels are that way, by the way.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:16.590
Hey!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:18.950
I'm home.

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:29.230
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, I'll be home late again tonight.
Eat dinner without me.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.050
"Geotechnics"

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.550
I love you, Mother.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:59.680
Don't say that. I know I'm not
your real mother, but you and I...

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.420
So what?

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.860
And what of your father? I can't betray him--

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.820
Excuse me.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.280
What do you want at this hour?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.850
My name is Takuya Arima.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:20.410
I want to get in touch 
with my mother, Ayumi...

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.790
She just left.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:24.700
Where did she go?

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.790
I can't tell anybody that. Even her son.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.590
Please!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:35.550
I know you take this job seriously,
and you're not the type to watch TV at work...

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.520
Mother!

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:37.960
No!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:42.720
She was on her way to a
scientific equipment leasing corporation.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.510
In the warehouse district at the port.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.310
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.360
Who are you people?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.110
Just like we said on the phone.
We're repairmen with the leasing company.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.940
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:00.490
It's not good to judge
people by their appearance.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.950
Now hand it over.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.450
Hand what over?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.910
Don't play dumb.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.320
The research data.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.130
Why are you doing this?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.260
Just hand it over.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.430
Unless you want to get hurt.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.010
Okay!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.470
Hey!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.480
Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.390
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, are you okay?

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:33.020
Was this guy in the script?

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.900
No, he's probably not part of the show.

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.790
I called the cops.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.940
You're bluffing.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.740
In five minutes, you'll find out.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.580
In five minutes, you won't have
an unbroken bone left in your body.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:46.980
Stop it!

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.330
I'll give you the data!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.120
So please don't hurt him!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:55.130
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, you don't need to give them that!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.990
No, Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.440
Don't do anything crazy... Please!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:04.680
Forget about the kid, lady.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.930
We're a lot more fun to hang out with.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.020
It's been a while since 
you've had a man, right?

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.020
I can tell by the look on your face.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.710
Cut it out, you bastards!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.410
Idiot.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.950
Takuya-<i>kun</i>! Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.560
Don't mess with professional brawlers, kid.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.250
You still want to do this?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.950
Yeah. Time for round 2.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.470
I can't do this unarmed.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:48.910
Hey!

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.730
Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.650
Ayumi-<i>san</i>, get out of here.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.360
Was this guy in the script?

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.150
No, he's probably not part of the show.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.210
Takuya-<i>kun</i>! Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.420
Don't mess with professional brawlers, kid.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.840
You still want to do this?

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:23.500
Yeah. I'm not the type who gives up.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.980
Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:36.480
Was this guy in the script?

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.480
No, he's probably not part of the show.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.490
--Takuya-<i>kun</i>! Takuya-<i>kun</i>!
--Gotcha...

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:49.060
Are you okay?

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.620
One more time...

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.500
Hold it!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:41.570
"Episode 3: Tears That Can't Be Stopped"

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:38.760
Episode 3: "Tears That Can't Be Stopped."
